# i18n and RTL

## Locale files

- Namespaced JSON: `src/locales/{ar,en}/common.json`, `home.json`, plus one file per new page
- Keep `ar` and `en` keys in parallel — same shape, always
- Wire new namespaces in `src/i18n.js`

## Usage in Vue

```vue
{{ t('home.hero.titlePrefix') }}
{{ t('common.nav.home') }}
```

- No hardcoded user-facing strings in templates or script
- Prefer existing key paths; extend namespaces instead of inventing parallel trees

## Direction and language

- Default locale: `ar` (fallback `en`)
- `src/main.js` / i18n sync `<html lang>` and `dir` (`rtl` for Arabic)
- Do not fight that system with one-off `dir` hacks unless fixing a real bug
